<title>JAPAN: New South Wales launches 5.6% yen/Aussie samurais.</title>
<headline>New South Wales launches 5.6% yen/Aussie samurais.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's New South Wales Treasury Corp launched 10 billion yen worth of 5.6 percent yen/Australian dollar samurai bonds due on October 25, 1999, on Tuesday, lead manager Nikko Securities said.</p>
<p>The bonds are priced at par, with coupon payments twice a year.</p>
<p>Holders of the samurai bonds will receive A$5,701.25 for each 500,000-yen bond held at maturity.</p>
<p>The coupon will be paid in yen, while redemption will be in Australian dollars.  </p>
<p>The terms are as follows.</p>
<p> AMT  10 bln yen	   COUPON 5.6 pct  MATURITY Oct 25, 1999</p>
<p> TYPE yen/Aussie samurai ISS PRICE par   PAY DATE Oct 25, 1996</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD  Oct 14 to Oct 24</p>
<p> INTEREST PAYMENT  April 25 and Oct 25</p>
<p> SIGN DATE  Oct 11</p>
<p> LAST RATING   Aa2(Moody's), AA(S&amp;P)</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER  Nikko Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE  Sanwa Bank</p>
</text>
